  "listen": "Good morning. This is The Daily Brief for Monday, October 12. The lead story is about Katie Zacharia, who has been named the new White House press secretary. NPR reports that she worked for one of Trump's companies and appeared often on conservative-leaning talk shows. The report describes her as a devoted fan of Trump and MAGA. Now to the other front page stories. Nearly 22 million dollars in taxpayer funds has been spent on ads, with about 10 million spent after Trump said a super PAC would fund them. In India, opposition parties marched to the top court as protests over voter list revisions escalate. Authorities have removed more than 130 million names from the voter roll. Ukraine says six energy sites have been hit by Russia since Trump announced an energy ceasefire. And NASA says Antarctic sea ice has reached its 2026 maximum, the third lowest since satellite records began. Now the sections. In Tech and AI, Python 3.15 is out, and Anthropic is expanding its Cyber Verification Program. In Politics, Drop Site News reports on India's crackdown on protesters, and NPR talks with Senator Jeanne Shaheen about the Russian diesel deal. In World, the BBC reports that actor RJ Mitte has died at age 34. Immigration agents searched the home of Congresswoman Ilhan Omar. In Sports, Brendan Allen won the UFC main event by fifth-round submission. The 49ers' Dre Greenlaw was suspended one game. In Atlanta, President Trump will campaign in Dalton on Friday with Rep. Mike Collins and Rick Jackson. Three modern homes are coming to market in Old Fourth Ward. In Architecture, Matterport now supports importing point cloud files, and IES Sync for Revit has launched. In Science and Nature, NASA will send experiments on human health and drug-resistant organisms to the space station. Wildfires on Borneo have left orangutans injured, and rescuers are evacuating them. That is the brief. Have a good day.",
